  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Ordinary typing and held-key actions",
      "items": [
        "layout.json defines 200 ms deliberate holds, home-row modifiers and mirrored action-layer triggers.",
        "generate.py emits native movement/selection shortcuts directly into Kanata. App/window layers emit named push-msg actions.",
        "macos.json maps portable movement names to macOS shortcuts and application names to bundle identifiers."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Two routes after a keypress",
      "items": [
        "Text or selection: Kanata emits native keyboard output through the virtual HID driver.",
        "App/window action: Kanata emits a TCP notification; the supervisor relays it to the authenticated user runner.",
        "The runner accepts only launch.* and the supported app/window cycling actions, then talks to the native helper over stdin/stdout.",
        "Kanata rejects mutating TCP commands. GUI automation runs as the signed-in user, with Accessibility permission."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "When capture is allowed",
      "items": [
        "starts if ready means: no persistent disable, connected runner, matching console user, approved virtual HID driver, and runner Accessibility permission.",
        "Root launchd jobs run the supervisor and matching driver; Home Manager creates the keyboard-actions user agent.",
        "The UNIX socket is restricted to the configured user; peer credentials authenticate requests. Runner registration and replies report permissions and health."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Failure returns to ordinary input",
      "items": [
        "The supervisor durably records disable before stopping capture on an engine exit, stream failure or runner failure.",
        "An active journal left by an interrupted supervisor also latches disable; KeepAlive is false rather than an unconditional restart loop.",
        "Physical Left Control+Space+Escape exits the engine; the supervisor records the exit as persistent disable.",
        "Recovery is explicit: keyboard status, keyboard permissions, and keyboard enable. Service startup does not clear intentional disable."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Build checks and evidence limits",
      "items": [
        "The Nix keyboard-support derivation generates kanata.kbd, runs kanata --check and executes test_keyboard.py with the patched simulator.",
        "test_lifecycle.py covers supervisor/runner behavior separately; operations.md describes when those checks are appropriate.",
        "This map traces committed source. It does not demonstrate live physical HID capture, the emergency chord, sleep/wake or device reconnection."
      ]
    }
  ]
